window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["26"]={"https://theconversation.com/minecraft-techno-raves-and-brainrot-are-modern-election-strategies-but-do-they-win-any-votes-296049":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"c3b49776728b9c700bfa3ca94f235c55f35d01c42e620abfcd082f2004e8c342","read":"https://theconversation.com/minecraft-techno-raves-and-brainrot-are-modern-election-strategies-but-do-they-win-any-votes-296049","bytes":179450,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Minecraft, techno raves and brainrot are modern election strategies, but do they win any votes?","by":[{"n":"Susan Grantham","r":"Senior Lecturer in Communication, Griffith University"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T18:23:51Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["What do Minecraft, brainrot and techno raves have in common? They have all been co-opted as political campaign strategies."]},{"k":"p","s":["With Victoria heading to the polls later this month, Victorian Labor has ventured into Minecraft, the video game where people build worlds out of blocks."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a reward for reaching 35,000 followers on Minecraft, Labor hosted a virtual party on TikTok featuring a Pauline Hanson diss track in phonk (a sub-genre of hip hop) style. Premier Ben Carroll even appeared to DJ on the TikTok live stream, though his button-pressing didn’t always seem to match the music."]},{"k":"p","s":["The event peaked at around 600 participants, with average attendance closer to 200. Which raises an obvious question: who exactly was this for?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Were young voters suddenly inspired to investigate Labor’s policies? Was it aimed at younger children whose parents might be potential Labor voters? Or was the real audience everyone watching clips of a politician pretending to DJ in a block-shaped universe?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Welcome to modern political campaigning, where winning the algorithm can sometimes seem more important than winning an argument."]},{"k":"h","s":["From Italian brainrot to political brainrot"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not the first time we have seen a trend-driven campaign. Labor famously used TikTok in its winning ",["2022 federal election campaign","https://doi.org/10.1080/22041451.2024.2349451"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["And, during ",["Australia’s 2025 federal election","https://theconversation.com/thought-the-election-campaign-was-boring-maybe-youre-just-not-on-tiktok-255847"],", the Liberal Party introduced voters to Tim Cheese, an AI-generated mouse complaining about the cost of living. There were ",["diss tracks, gaming memes","https://press-files.anu.edu.au/downloads/press/n14784/html/ch08.xhtml"]," and deliberately chaotic videos, presumably designed to speak the language of a younger audience."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is the world of brainrot: nonsensical, overstimulating internet content featuring everything from AI-generated animals to surreal characters speaking in strange voices."]},{"k":"p","s":["Italian brainrot involves bizarre AI-generated creatures with pseudo-Italian names, such as a crocodile crossed with a fighter jet named Bombardino Crocodilo. But add a political message and it gets very odd."]},{"k":"p","s":["The logic is understandable. Young people spend considerable time consuming short-form entertainment, so ",["political parties want to appear in those feeds","https://doi.org/10.1177/1329878X261501254"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But there’s a fine line between understanding internet culture and looking like someone’s dad attempting a TikTok dance at Christmas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Germany’s election gets even stranger"]},{"k":"p","s":["If Australia’s experiments seem unusual, Germany’s 2025 federal election provides some competition."]},{"k":"p","s":["A youth political group affiliated with the left-wing party Die Linke turned speeches by veteran politician Gregor Gysi into techno remixes, creating the unlikely phenomenon of DJ Gysi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Die Linke subsequently won ",["25% of the vote among 18–24-year-olds","https://www1.wdr.de/nachrichten/wahlergebnis-bundestagswahl-afd-linke-social-media-tiktok-100.html?"],". Whether the techno helped is not clear."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the other side of politics, the Alternative for Germany (AfD) Brandenberg branch posted a fully AI-generated advertisement depicting the future of Germany. This video included AI versions of rival party leaders Karl Lauterbach (Social Democratic Party) and Robert Habeck (Greens)."]},{"k":"p","s":["And ",["AI-generated influencers","https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-ai-influencers-targeting-german-elections/video-71514325"]," have begun spruiking political messages. This includes ",["Larissa Wagner","https://x.com/LarissaWagt"],", who is believed to have been created by a far-right group with connections to the American online magazine Compact."]},{"k":"p","s":["A TikTok creator also used the absurdist trend of talking AI animals to question the apparent contradiction between AfD leader Alice Weidel’s personal life and her party’s policies."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s political commentary delivered by a pigeon in a bathroom. And somehow, that makes perfect sense on TikTok."]},{"k":"p","s":[["German academic Marcus Bösch","https://tiktoktiktoktiktok.substack.com/p/brainrot-as-anti-content"]," argues brainrot isn’t simply meaningless entertainment. Its absurdity can make political messages easier to circulate, often disguised through humour and irony."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s a little like hiding the vegetables in a toddler’s dinner, except the vegetables are political ideology and the dinner is an AI-generated pigeon."]},{"k":"p","s":["The danger is that repeated exposure can make even troubling political imagery appear familiar, without anyone necessarily engaging with the ideas behind it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Politics has entered the rave"]},{"k":"p","s":["Britain’s Greens party has taken the word “party” literally, moving political campaigning onto actual dance floors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since January, a grassroots collective called ",["Green Space","https://www.greenspace.community/parties"],", created by Greens members, has been organising political raves, complete with DJs, dancefloors and appearances from party leader Zack Polanski."]},{"k":"p","s":["Its first London event attracted around 1,400 revellers and raised £13,000 (A$25,000), while a ",["subsequent Leeds rave","https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/apr/20/greens-zack-polanski-rave-club-night-appearance-leeds"]," drew more than 2,000 and is estimated to have raised £16,000 (A$31,000). That is considerably more tangible than a few thousand video views."]},{"k":"p","s":["It also highlights an important distinction. A nightclub fundraiser can create community, recruit volunteers and generate money, particularly in a world where we are ",["craving real connection","https://doi.org/10.1177/1329878X261472218"],", both face-to-face and virtually."]},{"k":"h","s":["When the meme becomes the message"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political parties are increasingly trying to inhabit a world, described by journalist and social commentator Kieran Press-Reynolds as “ ",["Shitpostmodernism","https://spikeartmagazine.com/articles/essay-shitpostmodernism"],"”. It is an internet of fragmented trends, absurd humour and rapidly changing cultural references."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of course, there’s nothing wrong with politicians having fun. ",["Humour can make politics","https://doi.org/10.1177/1329878X251327232"]," more accessible, while engaging with online culture can reach people who would never attend a traditional political event."]},{"k":"p","s":["But visibility, engagement and influence are very different things. Someone might share a politician’s Minecraft performance because they love it, hate it, or simply cannot believe it’s happening. None necessarily translates into a vote."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps Victorian Labor’s Minecraft party introduced politics to an entirely new audience. Or perhaps 200 people just enjoyed some phonk while a politician enthusiastically pressed buttons."]},{"k":"p","s":["Either way, the question remains: are politicians getting better at communicating with young people, or just getting better at entertaining them?"]}],"chars":5852},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/austria":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"cc0aaf3d39afc8381e69916c97a24ff0da7f974747df43eb94a4dc8944aa7949","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/austria","bytes":74710,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Austria travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:19:06+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/austria/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Austria set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Austrian Embassy in the UK","https://www.bmeia.gv.at/en/austrian-embassy-london/about-us/map-and-opening-hours/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Austria follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport if you need to","https://www.gov.uk/apply-renew-passport"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel without a visa to the Schengen area, which includes Austria, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The requirements for ",["working in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-austria-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Schengen countries within the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Austrian border control, you may need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel booking confirmation or proof of address for a second home"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your travel insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Austrian government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Austrian Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://www.bmeia.gv.at/en/travel-stay/entrance-and-residence-in-austria/"]," or the ",["Austrian Embassy in the UK","https://www.bmeia.gv.at/en/austrian-embassy-london/travelling-to-austria/entry-requirements-visa-and-immigration/schengen-visa-application-requirements/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Austria with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-austria#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border controls at Germany’s land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are temporary border controls in place to travel into Germany. Check the ",["entry requirements for Germany","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/germany/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Austria","https://www.bmf.gv.at/en/topics/customs/travellers/entry-from-non-eu-countries.html"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Austria."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["national and international transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["music, sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["entertainment establishments and nightlife venues"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings and international institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship and religious sites"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should be vigilant in public places and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent examples include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 15 February 2025, one person was killed and five injured in central Villach, Carinthia, southern Austria in a knife attack"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 2 November 2020, four people were killed and 23 injured in a terrorism-related shooting in central Vienna"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Austrian authorities have successfully disrupted various attack plans, making a number of arrests in recent years. You can expect to see an increased police presence, and additional safety measures may be in place. Be aware of your surroundings and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations may happen with little or no warning in cities. Follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are generally low. However, there are higher levels of petty crime, particularly pickpocketing, in the big city centres and city parks after dark. Thieves use a variety of methods to distract people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care on public transport and in crowded city centres, including main stations. Be particularly careful with your belongings on international trains and when you take your baggage from trains and coaches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinks served in bars overseas are often stronger than those in the UK. Be careful about taking drinks from strangers or leaving your drinks unattended. Criminals have robbed and assaulted people after spiking their drinks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["By law, you must always have easy access to your passport. If you do not carry your passport, you must be able to get it quickly. It can be helpful to carry a copy of the photo page. The Austrian authorities do not accept a UK driving licence as official ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Austria have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Face-covering ban"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s generally illegal to wear any clothing or object in public that covers your face. You could get a fine of up to 150 euros. See ",["information on Austria’s face-covering ban","https://www.oesterreich.gv.at/en/themen/menschen_aus_anderen_staaten/aufenthalt/Seite.120251"],", including a list of exemptions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must validate your ticket in a ticket machine before starting a journey on public transport. If you do not, you could get a 100 to 500 euro on-the-spot fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["For outdoor activities and adventure sports, make sure:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you use a well-established company"]},{"k":"li","s":["your insurance covers your specific activity"]},{"k":"p","s":["For sports activities like skiing, potholing and mountaineering, and for sports classed as particularly dangerous (for example, off-piste skiing, mountain biking, climbing or paragliding), your insurance should include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mountain rescue services"]},{"k":"li","s":["helicopter costs"]},{"k":"li","s":["repatriation to your country of residence"]},{"k":"li","s":["transfer to neighbouring countries for treatment"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check weather forecasts and conditions. Make sure you’re properly equipped for the worst-case scenario with items such as a map, compass, GPS and telecommunications equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Adventure sports and activities are riskier if you’re alone. Consider hiring a guide for expert advice. Always leave details of your itinerary with someone."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Skiing"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["preparing for winter sports abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/winter-sports-stay-safe-on-the-slopes"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take advice on weather and avalanche conditions before you travel. Follow local skiing laws and regulations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Off-piste skiing is very dangerous and can invalidate your travel insurance. Avalanches are a risk in some areas. Follow safety instructions carefully and go with a qualified guide. See ",["European Avalanche Warning Service","https://www.avalanches.org/"]," and the Austrian Avalanche Warning Service (in German)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Austria, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Austria guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/austria/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving laws in Austria can be complex, especially for caravan and motorhomes. For more information, see EU road rules and safety and ",["Austrian vehicle laws","https://www.oesterreich.gv.at/en/themen/mobilitaet/kfz/10"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Austria if you are aged 18 or over. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Austria, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience and a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry insurance and vehicle ownership documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on driving if you’re living in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-austria#driving-in-austria"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Motorway tolls"]},{"k":"p","s":["All vehicles on motorways and expressways in Austria are subject to tolls. If you use Austrian motorways, you must ",["display a vignette (sticker)","https://www.austria.info/en/service-and-facts/getting-there-around/by-car/vignette"]," inside your windscreen. You could get a fine if you do not."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Austria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/16/austria#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Austria","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/16/austria#General_Information"],", including tick-borne diseases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Austria. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/austria-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Austria, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-austria#healthcare"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services Austria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance or rescue: 144"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 122"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 133"]},{"k":"p","s":["European emergency number: 112"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also download the ",["112 Where Are U app","https://where.areu.lombardia.it/"],", the European emergency number app."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?country=Austria&serviceType=lawyers"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Austria"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters"]," in Austria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guide-for-austria"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/austria-prisoner-pack-austrian-prison-rules/information-pack-for-british-nationals-arrested-or-detained-in-austria"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/austria/british-embassy-vienna"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/austria/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Austria","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-austria"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":16632,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/whats-missing-from-election-promises-in-victorias-rural-health-debate-a-long-term-vision-294358":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"f33cafc3de11a1fddd03fcc78e836962c62c6262d4c1bc2dfe2d354e2b4f58b1","read":"https://theconversation.com/whats-missing-from-election-promises-in-victorias-rural-health-debate-a-long-term-vision-294358","bytes":186538,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What’s missing from election promises in Victoria’s rural health debate? A long-term vision","by":[{"n":"Belinda O'Sullivan","r":"Professor and Director of Research, Monash Rural Health, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T04:15:11Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Some of Victoria’s ",["fastest-growing communities","https://www.infrastructurevictoria.com.au/topics/regional-victoria"]," are in regional areas. About ",["1.6 million people","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/population/regional-population"]," already call regional Victoria home. With ",["data centres","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-01-22/keppel-data-centre-latrobe-valley/106123748"]," and ",["major renewable energy projects","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-15/warracknabeal-wind-farm-clears-victorian-approvals/107263312"]," slated for development across the state, this number is set to grow further."]},{"k":"p","s":["A growing population will place increasing demands on already strained rural health-care services. People in these communities have a breadth of health needs, and we need preventative, primary health care and hospital care that works for all of them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unfortunately, that isn’t the reality on the ground, something which has become a key issue ahead of Victoria’s state election."]},{"k":"p","s":["In February, the Rural Doctor’s Association of Victoria ",["called on","https://rdav.com.au/VIC/_Vic/News/Vic-Articles/Fair%20deal%20urged%20for%20rural%20patients%20in%20state%20election.aspx"]," Victoria’s major parties to commit to ending the state’s “inequitable health system”."]},{"k":"p","s":["And late last month, Victorian doctors ",["demanded","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/state-election/dont-get-sick-in-vic-doctors-launch-election-campaign-targeting-broken-health-system/news-story/641c145c6b0fb3635a98d068367d054c"]," all parties fix the state’s broken health system, launching their “Don’t get sick in Vic” campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, just over two weeks out from polling day, major parties are offering only short-term and simplistic solutions, without any real overarching strategy to improve health care for rural communities. Here’s why – and what practical, lasting solutions could look like."]},{"k":"h","s":["The postcode problem"]},{"k":"p","s":["The challenges facing rural Victoria reflect a nationwide problem. Despite paying the same taxes, where Australians live can make a significant difference to the quality of health care they receive."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to an October ",["report","https://www.ruralhealth.org.au/publication/the-forgotten-health-spend-a-report-on-the-expenditure-deficit-in-rural-australia-2026/"]," by the National Rural Health Alliance, Australians living outside major cities receive about A$1,200 less per person per year across health, disability and aged-care spending."]},{"k":"p","s":["The health system in rural Victoria has yet to recover from the COVID pandemic. The loss of migratory health workers led to significant pressures on general practices and allied health businesses."]},{"k":"p","s":["The funding and training of general practitioners (GPs) is primarily the responsibility of the federal government. But GPs play a major role in the health of rural Victorians, crossing over into disability, aged care and rural hospitals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many GPs are choosing to ",["retire","https://www.racgp.org.au/getmedia/80c8bdc9-8886-4055-8a8d-ea793b088e5a/Health-of-the-Nation.pdf"]," early. Those who have remained are more selective about their workloads. A ",["2024 study","https://www1.racgp.org.au/ajgp/2024/supplement-december/burnout-and-retention-of-general-practice-supervis"]," of Australian GP supervisors suggested almost 80% have high exhaustion rates."]},{"k":"p","s":["A separate ",["2025 Australian survey","https://gpsa.org.au/research-and-policy/2025-national-survey-report/"]," found less than half (44%) said they were willing to supervise trainee doctors in the next ",["five","https://gpsa.org.au/research-and-policy/2025-national-survey-report/"]," years. This may limit how many new doctors can be trained in rural Victoria."]},{"k":"p","s":["Election promises purporting to boost rural doctor numbers – such as health worker ",["incentive schemes","https://vic.nationals.org.au/media-releases/jade-benham-mp-nationals-and-liberals-set-to-boost-regional-health-workforce/"]," – do not address how we keep them once training is over."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why promising more hospital beds alone isn’t enough"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ahead of the Victorian state election, both ",["Labor","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-25/vic-labor-campaign-launch-health-hospital-investment/107304732"]," and the ",["Coalition","https://www.vicliberal.org.au/article/strengthen-our-health-system"]," have pledged a mix of more timely emergency services, surgery, beds and health workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such promises centre on acute care, but do little to shift the dial for rural health unless they are paired with investment in grassroots general health care."]},{"k":"p","s":["In many smaller communities – particularly where access to specialist doctors is limited or requires lengthy travel – rural generalists play a vital role. These are GPs with extra training to provide complementary care across emergency, obstetrics, anaesthetics, paediatrics and palliative care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Interestingly, despite declining interest in specialising in general practice, there has been ",["growing interest","https://www.racgp.org.au/health-of-the-nation-2026/future-workforce/gps-in-training#:%7E:text=In%202025%2C%20only%208.8%25%20of%20medical%20students,for%20future%20practice%20ranks%20fourth%20(Figure%2041)"]," among medical students to specialise as a rural generalist since 2021."]},{"k":"p","s":["This presents a significant opportunity. Victoria already co-invests in the federal government’s ",["rural generalist training program","https://www.vicruralgeneralist.com.au/"],". The state could capitalise further by exploring how to create attractive and sustainable employment options for rural generalists in rural hospitals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Breaking down barriers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drawing on interviews with people involved in training and employing rural generalist doctors across Victoria, my own ",["previous research","https://doi.org/10.1111/ajr.70019"]," has examined what helps attract rural generalists to regional areas, and what makes them stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["We found several barriers. These included health services competing for a limited number of doctors, competition with other specialists, varying levels of support from hospital leaders, and problems with workforce planning."]},{"k":"p","s":["But we also identified promising solutions, including having a clear statewide plan for the rural workforce, improving coordination between different regional health services, and improving recognition and pay for rural generalists themselves."]},{"k":"h","s":["More specialists, closer to home"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rural generalists, however, don’t replace specialists; they complement them. Many rural Victorians with chronic conditions are being hit with ",["significant costs","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-15/vptas-regional-victoria-government-healthcare-access/107263272"]," to travel to Melbourne, not to mention the time lost travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["This points to the need to invest in more rural specialist training in our regions, to grow more specialists closer to home. Any new state investment in regional specialist training positions would build on the work of rural clinical schools."]},{"k":"p","s":["These institutions, with Commonwealth support, ",["select and train people from rural areas","https://doi.org/10.1111/medu.14069"]," to realise their dream of working in their own community as rural paediatricians, obstetricians and palliative care specialists. But they can’t stay if all the training is in the city."]},{"k":"h","s":["Allied health is missing from the debate"]},{"k":"p","s":["Any funding rethink should also apply to allied health and ",["multidisciplinary care","https://www.health.vic.gov.au/cancer-treatment/multidisciplinary-care"],". Allied health encompasses professionals working in a wide range of roles, including physios, occupational therapists, psychologists, speech pathologists and social workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["It has a central role keeping people moving, thinking and socially engaged. Delivered well, it also helps prevent avoidable hospital readmissions and facilitates better care for staying healthy at home, along with promoting early discharge."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional Victoria currently faces a chronic deficit in rural allied health professionals and care coordinators. This is compounded by declining volunteerism and long waiting times for home care and aged care packages. And the consequences spill directly into our public emergency departments as bed-block and ambulance ramping."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, in this year’s election debate, allied health has hardly been mentioned as a solution to ",["emergency care and ambulance ramping","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-25/vic-labor-campaign-launch-health-hospital-investment/107304732"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["A coordinated approach to rural health"]},{"k":"p","s":["We’ll have to wait and see who forms the next Victorian state government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whoever does, perhaps the most important opportunity to improve rural health care is to build on investments by the federal government. And “go bold” on setting a vision for rural workforce and health service planning."]},{"k":"p","s":["A wide range of groups – the Rural Workforce Agency, rural Primary Health Networks, regional hospital networks and universities and colleges – can help inform this approach."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are a lot of voters living outside Melbourne. That means a big opportunity for the party with a strategic, engaged plan to improve rural health."]}],"chars":6873},"https://theconversation.com/why-quebec-separatism-is-unlikely-despite-the-parti-quebecois-election-win-295646":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"d69b7cc4038346b6c5c584d2cc3acdffb280db20e809e1b00ec0625faf0f646d","read":"https://theconversation.com/why-quebec-separatism-is-unlikely-despite-the-parti-quebecois-election-win-295646","bytes":188024,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Why Québec separatism is unlikely despite the Parti Québecois election win","by":[{"n":"Gavin Furrey","r":"Assistant Professor, Political Science, Université du Québec à Montréal (UQAM)"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T14:31:48Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Québec’s flagship sovereignist party, ",["the Parti Québecois (PQ), formed a minority government","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/crly09gz7ew4o"]," in the recent provincial election. The party essentially rose from the dead after a 12-year absence, dethroning the right-wing nationalist — but not separatist — Coalition Avenir Québec (CAQ)."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Canadians, the PQ is typically associated with sovereignty referendums. Yet, despite the PQ victory, ",["estimates place Québecois support for sovereignty at between 27 and 31 per cent","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/montreal/quebec-parti-quebecois-electoral-reform-9.7373016"],", a far cry from the ",["49.42 per cent who voted to separate in the 1995 referendum","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2025/10/27/30-years-quebec-referendum-1995/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This figure aligns somewhat with the popular vote received by the PQ, which, at 28 per cent, is ",["the lowest popular vote share of a sitting government in the history of the province","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/montreal/quebec-parti-quebecois-electoral-reform-9.7373016"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The PQ’s victory therefore should be understood in light of three factors: low public support for the PQ and for separatism, Indigenous resistance to Québec independence and a global context where statehood doesn’t necessarily shield against interference or expand diplomatic leverage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Lukewarm mood on independence"]},{"k":"p","s":["The combination of Québec’s multi-party system and its “first-past-the-post” electoral system means governments are often formed on less than a majority of the popular vote."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In six elections between 2007–2022, an average of 53.9 per cent of votes failed to translate into seats","https://www.mercedezroberge.ca/5-les-votes-perdus-un-trait-de-caractere-du-systeme-majoritaire/?utm_"],", according to electoral expert Mercédez Roberge."]},{"k":"p","s":["This explains how the separatist PQ was able to form government despite the measured lack of enthusiasm for separatism in the province."]},{"k":"p","s":["In fact, even leaving room for the possibility that leftist ",["Québec Solidaire","https://quebecsolidaire.net/"]," supporters also support independence (though the party does not necessarily prioritize it), a combination of the popular votes earned by parties that explicitly do not support independence suggests that ",["58.24 per cent of the electorate don’t want to separate from Canada.","https://www.electionsquebec.qc.ca/en/results-and-statistics/general-election-results/2026-10-05/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["PQ leader Paul St-Pierre Plamondon’s statements following his party’s victory reflects a generally lukewarm mood towards independence in the province. During his campaign, Plamondon mitigated his promise to hold a referendum during his first term by stating it wouldn’t be held while Donald Trump remained president of the United States."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the meantime, ",["Plamondon has prioritized housing and cost of living issues, and has signalled to the English-speaking community that “we’re all in the same boat.”","https://globalnews.ca/news/12090600/pq-leader-plamondon-referendum-quebec/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Plamondon’s prudence is paired with various assertions of Québec autonomy."]},{"k":"p","s":["In his first month as premier, he’s ",["antagonized the federal government by skipping the recent Canada-European Union summit","https://www.ctvnews.ca/montreal/article/quebec-premier-paul-st-pierre-plamondon-to-skip-canada-eu-summit/"],". ",["Under the CAQ, antagonism was more often directed at Québec’s increasingly ethnically and religiously diverse population","https://www.puq.ca/catalogue/themes/pensee-federaliste-contemporaine-quebec-3833.html"],". ",["Without dropping this inward-facing orientation to nation-building","https://pq.org/nouvelles/le-parti-quebecois-sengage-a-defendre-le-consensus-quebecois-sur-la-laicite/"],", the PQ’s swipes at Ottawa suggests it will return to stoking more familiar Québec-Ottawa tensions."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in a country with longstanding debates about provincial autonomy, none of this is new or indicative of separatist sentiments. The recent PQ victory is more akin to detecting a faint pulse in a terminally ill patient than a spectacular jolt back to life."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Unruly provinces? That’s what the Fathers of Confederation expected — and planned for","https://theconversation.com/unruly-provinces-thats-what-the-fathers-of-confederation-expected-and-planned-for-192306"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Changed scene from 1995"]},{"k":"p","s":["The PQ has formed a government in a situation different from 1995."]},{"k":"p","s":["Domestically, First Nations have increasingly affirmed their place in Canada’s tapestry. In 1996, the Royal Commission on Aboriginal Peoples published ",["its five-volume, 4,000-page report making 440 recommendations","https://publications.gc.ca/Pilot/LoPBdP/EB/prb9924-e.htm"],". Among them were recognizing Indigenous Peoples as ",["self-governing nations and creating Indigenous institutions","https://www.rcaanc-cirnac.gc.ca/eng/1100100014597/1572547985018"],", including an Indigenous parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2015, the Truth and Reconciliation Commission published its final report, which included ",["94 calls to action to address the harms of the residential school system and advance reconciliation across areas that include child welfare, education, health, justice and culture","https://nctr.ca/about/truth-and-reconciliation-commission-of-canada-calls-to-action/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The following year, Canada officially adopted the United Nations Declaration for the Rights of Indigenous Peoples. ",["The document became federal law in 2021","https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/declaration/about-apropos.html"],". Finally, since 1995, ",["at least 19 modern treaties have been concluded or come into effect","https://www.rcaanc-cirnac.gc.ca/eng/1677073191939/1677073214344"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It would be misleading to claim, however, that the relationship between Canadian governments and Indigenous nations has radically changed in the last 30 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plamondon’s absence from ",["the First Nations-First Ministers meeting recently held in Ottawa","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2026/10/27/indigenous-leaders-quebec-premier-skips-first-nations-meeting/"]," is an example. Québec’s minister responsible for relations with First Nations and Inuit wrote that ",["the premier’s absence was aimed at prioritizing direct nation-to-nation meetings with Indigenous nations on “notre territoire","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2026/10/27/indigenous-leaders-quebec-premier-skips-first-nations-meeting/"]," (‘our territory.’)”"]},{"k":"p","s":["This phrasing takes Québec’s territorial sovereignty as a given, treating it as a non-negotiable precondition that other nations must accept before dialogue can even begin. By prioritizing provincial self-determination, it implicitly subordinates Indigenous sovereignty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Claiming these talks are “nation-to-nation” rings hollow when one party unilaterally dictates the terms of engagement."]},{"k":"p","s":["The premier’s decision to skip the meeting was ",["criticized by the Assembly of First Nations of Québec and Labrador (AFNQL) and the Native Women’s Shelter of Montréal","https://montreal.citynews.ca/2026/10/27/indigenous-leaders-quebec-premier-skips-first-nations-meeting/"],", who wanted Québec to be at the table in Ottawa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plamondon would do well to remember that in 1995, ",["multiple First Nations within Québec’s boundaries refused forcible inclusion into a new independent state","https://publications.gc.ca/Collection-R/LoPBdP/BP/bp412-e.htm#:%7E:text=The%20Crees%20have%20asserted%20for,keep%20their%20territory%20in%20Canada."],", notably those whose rivers provide ",["the bulk of the province’s hydroelectricity","https://nunatsiaq.com/stories/article/did-you-know-fast-facts-about-the-james-bay-hydroelectric-project/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Modern risks of independent statehood"]},{"k":"p","s":["Internationally, ",["separatist sentiments today have more to do with populism","https://theconversation.com/in-alberta-far-right-populism-fuelled-by-conspiracy-theories-and-alienation-drive-bid-to-separate-from-canada-294374"]," than with the decolonization efforts that played out in the second half of the 20th century. In a climate of ",["survival-of-the-fittest foreign policy","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cmly016ep243o"],", sovereignty in the form of an independent state does not guarantee the same freedoms or capacities it might have in 1980 and 1995."]},{"k":"p","s":["As U.K. political scientist ",["Michael Keating suggests, self-determination is no longer fixed to a single people or territory","https://doi.org/10.1080/17449057.2019.1585093"],". Nations today are largely regarded as contested constructs, and territories are multi-layered with various cultural and ethnic populations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Additionally, sovereignty doesn’t shield a state from the decisions of another, as recent American tariff policies are showing Canadians all too well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["3 ways Canada can navigate an increasingly erratic and belligerent United States","https://theconversation.com/3-ways-canada-can-navigate-an-increasingly-erratic-and-belligerent-united-states-276035"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Keating’s argument aligns with ",["Indigenous political theories of relational autonomy","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/319456880_What_is_a_treaty_On_contract_and_mutual_aid"],": today sovereignty is experienced less as something a nation possesses and more as a continuously negotiated relationship."]},{"k":"p","s":["American threats to Canadian sovereignty and Greenland’s self-determination suggests that secession would not necessarily improve upon Québec’s ability to negotiate its position within the broader international order."]},{"k":"p","s":["In short, in a world where even ",["the U.S., a superpower for decades, is experiencing the costs of fractured relationships","https://doi.org/10.53532/ss.038.04.00129"],", a convincing pitch for Québec separatism would have to take into account similar costs. The pulse of Québec separatism persists, though the body sustaining it is weighed down by internal fractures and a punishing political landscape."]}],"chars":7164}};
